explanation of each component:
app.py: This file is used to load known data for training the regression model and provides an interface via the Flask API for inputting the independent variable parameters w and x and outputting the predicted observed stakeholder engagement score.
Dockerfile: Used to build container images to ensure consistency in the user's environment. Containerization enables code to run stably in any Docker-enabled environment, thereby improving code reproducibility and deployment efficiency.
Requirements.txt: lists all the required Python dependencies to ensure that the project can install the required version of libraries in different environments and avoid version conflicts.
How containerization improves reproducibility of results: because the version of the python package is specified and docker is used to package all the necessary components into a single image to avoid differences in results due to host differences.

